WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:02.335
♪ (EERIE MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:00:09.041 --> 00:00:10.210
(SCREAMS)

00:00:13.579 --> 00:00:15.882
(BABY CRIES)

00:00:15.982 --> 00:00:17.517
Imagine if a baby fell
out the sky

00:00:17.617 --> 00:00:18.585
and fell into your arms.

00:00:18.685 --> 00:00:19.552
What would you be thinking?

00:00:25.791 --> 00:00:27.560
Open the bag for me, miss.

00:00:29.962 --> 00:00:31.264
(BABY COOS)

00:00:32.098 --> 00:00:32.966
(LOUD CRASH)

00:00:33.066 --> 00:00:34.299
Fuck.

00:00:34.566 --> 00:00:36.669
Imagine a woman,
never wanted a child,

00:00:36.769 --> 00:00:37.570
in her mid-30s,

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:39.539
searching for something
in her life,

00:00:39.639 --> 00:00:40.506
 but it isn't a baby.

00:00:40.606 --> 00:00:42.608
I wanted
the audience's first impression

00:00:42.709 --> 00:00:45.411
to really be what mine was,
of like, "Wow."

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:47.546
 And that it's a comedy-horror,
 you know.

00:00:47.646 --> 00:00:49.516
I just love the combination
of genres.

00:00:49.816 --> 00:00:51.251
Can I leave this with you?

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:55.688
We came up with the show
when we were traveling

00:00:55.788 --> 00:00:56.956
a couple of years ago.

00:00:57.056 --> 00:00:58.524
The idea kind of
fell out of the sky.

00:00:58.624 --> 00:01:01.327
 It just felt like a kind of
 wacky comedy-horror premise.

00:01:01.994 --> 00:01:03.262
 And then as the story evolved,

00:01:03.362 --> 00:01:04.397
 and through
 the development process,

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:06.165
 we kind of realized
 that actually it was becoming

00:01:06.266 --> 00:01:08.668
 more and more about
 the deep ambivalence

00:01:08.768 --> 00:01:12.438
that we both were feeling about
whether we would become parents.

00:01:12.805 --> 00:01:15.308
I think I've forgotten
how normal people behave.

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:17.543
SIÂN ROBINS-GRACE: I guess
 one of the big themes is love,

00:01:17.643 --> 00:01:20.046
 and the way we're kind of told
 we should love each other,

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:21.848
 and the ways we actually do.

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:24.484
The main theme's sisterhood,

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:26.285
just sort of family
and community,

00:01:26.386 --> 00:01:28.020
 and mothering and motherhood.

00:01:28.387 --> 00:01:30.622
The show is centered
around three women,

00:01:30.723 --> 00:01:34.026
 Natasha, her sister Bobbi,
 and Mrs. Eaves.

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:36.362
Bobbi's a real people pleaser.

00:01:36.462 --> 00:01:38.231
She's a real bubbly person.

00:01:39.798 --> 00:01:40.800
Macadamia nut?

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:42.001
No.

00:01:42.668 --> 00:01:43.769
AMIRA GHAZALLA: Mrs. Eaves,
 I think she's very unique.

00:01:43.869 --> 00:01:47.139
There is so much courage
in the way the story's written,

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:48.307
 and the way we're telling it.

00:01:48.774 --> 00:01:51.544
MICHELLE DE SWARTE: I think
 it's a real compassionate,

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:57.217
funny, scary, dark,
enlightening look at motherhood.

00:01:58.117 --> 00:01:59.219
You had a baby?

00:02:00.352 --> 00:02:01.955
But you don't--
you don't want a baby.

00:02:02.722 --> 00:02:04.691
AMBER GRAPPY: It's light,
 and it's fun sometimes,

00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:06.759
and equally scary and dark.

00:02:06.859 --> 00:02:09.862
It just has so much versatility.

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:12.998
It's a totally original show.

00:02:13.499 --> 00:02:16.168
Come, be ready to laugh,
and be a bit frightened.

00:02:16.268 --> 00:02:17.470
Connect to some
of the characters

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:19.105
and connect to some
of the stories.

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:20.373
Ta-da!

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:23.509
And hopefully have a bit
to think about

00:02:23.609 --> 00:02:25.478
in terms of mothering
and motherhood.

00:02:25.578 --> 00:02:27.914
♪ (EERIE MUSIC CONTINUES) ♪

